contentText:
Chino Pacas is stepping into the action. The 19-year-old música Mexicana star releases his third studio album, Que Sigan Llegando Las Pacas V2 , on Thursday (Sept. 3) via Street Mob Records — a 13-track, genre-hopping set steeped in revenge, love, ambition and a sleek John Wick-inspired universe.

It’s a new chapter for the Guanajuato-born artist, who was named to Billboard ’s 2026 21 Under 21 list after breaking through with his unflinching corridos. On V2 , Chino stretches that foundation in every direction: There are corridos and cumbia, hip-hop turns and hyperpop detours, plus appearances from Fuerza Regida on “Te Digo” and Mexican artist FLVCKKA on “Madrugada,” the only single released ahead of the album. The album also features labelmate Calle 24 on &#8220;Bonita.&#8221;

