The project’s focal point is “Envidia,” which comes with an accompanying mini-movie-style video that channels the world of the legendary fictional hitman and antihero. “We made a short film based on the plot of John Wick ,” Chino tells Billboard . “Whenever I listened to this song, I always imagined this.” Beyond the action, it was the film’s visual language — “the theme, the costumes” — and the image of John Wick facing enemies from all sides that connected with him.

That cinematic world gives Chino room to reveal sides of himself that don’t always fit inside a traditional corrido. “These new songs allow me to express myself in a way that isn’t possible in a corrido,” he says. “In hyperpop, I can really immerse myself.”

Chino adds: “I’ve achieved many of the goals I had from the beginning, and now those goals have expanded and become much bigger.&#8221; He hopes the album highlights “the versatility that allows me to grow as a musician and songwriter.”

